// data/affinity_corpus.jsonc — committed affinity corpus for the `embedded` draft-pool variant.
//
// GENERATED FILE. The JSON body below is regenerated by
// `npm run bake-affinity-corpus` — do not hand-edit it. (This comment header IS
// preserved across re-bakes, so notes added here are safe.)
//
// WHAT THIS IS
//   The draft-record-derived card-by-card synergy the `embedded` variant grows
//   from: a play-rate `prior` plus a sparse `affinity` matrix in index space
//   (each entry [sourceIndex, [[targetIndex, value], ...]] indexes into `cards`).
//   Floats are rounded to 6 decimals — the precision at which this matrix
//   reproduces the live `sigseed` generator's pools byte-for-byte. Because it IS
//   the matrix `sigseed` builds from records (with the overlay folded in), the
//   `embedded` variant draws exactly the same pools as `sigseed` while letting
//   new and changed cards be authored in the overlay.
//
// HOW IT WAS GENERATED  (scripts/bake-affinity-corpus.mjs)
//   1. Build the base record-derived affinity corpus (buildPickfitCorpus) from
//      the bundled draft records in public/draft-records-data.json.
//   2. Fold in the committed "resembles" recipes from data/affinity_overlay.jsonc.
//   3. Round and serialize the sparse matrix. The bake has no randomness, so the
//      same records + overlay reproduce this body byte-for-byte.
//
// HOW TO UPDATE IT
//   1. Edit data/affinity_overlay.jsonc to add or re-point a card (and, for
//      build-around metric credit, data/buildaround_support.json).
//   2. Re-bake and refresh the served copy:
//        npm run bake-affinity-corpus     # rewrites this file (header preserved)
//        npm run setup-assets             # copies it to public/affinity-corpus-data.json (comments stripped)
//   3. Validate:  npm run affinity-corpus-parity
//   4. Commit this file together with data/affinity_overlay.jsonc.
//   When fresh drafts land in docs/draft_records_adapted/, re-run setup-assets
//   then bake to rebuild from the larger record set; the overlay recipes re-apply
//   automatically. See docs/cards2/affinity_embedding_workflow.md.
